{"id":"azure-bgp-oscillation-route-leak","benchmark":"skillsbench","instruction":"Detect BGP route oscillation and leaks in an Azure Virtual WAN network topology and evaluate which solutions can fix them.\n\nInput explanations:\n- route.json: the route advertised from vnet\n- preferences.json: routing preferences between hubs\n- local_pref.json: relationship type weight\n\nSteps:\n1. Load input files in `/app/data/`\n2. Detect in the topology: oscillation and/or route leak event violating BGP valley-free routing\n3. When oscillation or route leaks are detected, evaluate the possible solutions in the input. Load `possible_solutions.json`. For each solution, determine if it resolves oscillation and/or route leaks. To resolve oscillations, it must break the routing preference cycle in topology. To resolve route leaks, it must stop hub1/hub2 advertising routes to hub2/hub1 via Virtual Wan\n4. Save result to `/app/output/oscillation_report.json` using the format below\n\n```json\n{\n  \"oscillation_detected\": true,\n  \"oscillation_cycle\": [65002, 65003],\n  \"affected_ases\": [65002, 65003],\n  \"route_leak_detected\": true,\n  \"route_leaks\": [\n    {\n      \"leaker_as\": 65002,\n      \"source_as\": 65001,\n      \"destination_as\": 65003,\n      \"source_type\": \"provider\",\n      \"destination_type\": \"peer\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"solution_results\": {\n    \"Change BGP keepalive timer of vhubvnet1 to 30 seconds and holdtime to 90 seconds\": {\n      \"oscillation_resolved\": false,\n      \"route_leak_resolved\": true\n    }\n  }\n}\n```","supplemental":[],"items":[{"item_id":"OUT-01","requirement":"Write the result as valid JSON to /app/output/oscillation_report.json containing exactly the six top-level keys oscillation_detected, oscillation_cycle, affected_ases, route_leak_detected, route_leaks, and solution_results.","source_quote":"Save result to `/app/output/oscillation_report.json` using the format below","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestDetection::test_output_structure","verification":"A grader can verify this by loading /app/output/oscillation_report.json as JSON and confirming it is a dict containing all six required keys.","notes":"File existence itself is enforced transitively by the module-scoped output_data fixture, which every test depends on.","validation":{"item_id":"OUT-01","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"OSC-01","requirement":"Correctly detect the routing-preference oscillation in the topology by setting oscillation_detected to true and listing the ASNs involved in the oscillating cycle (65002 and 65003) in oscillation_cycle.","source_quote":"Detect in the topology: oscillation and/or route leak event violating BGP valley-free routing","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestDetection::test_oscillation_detected","verification":"A grader can verify this by checking output_data['oscillation_detected'] is true and that both 65002 and 65003 appear in output_data['oscillation_cycle'].","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"OSC-01","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"OSC-02","requirement":"Populate affected_ases with the AS numbers impacted by the detected oscillation cycle, consistent with the oscillation_cycle values.","source_quote":"\"affected_ases\": [65002, 65003],","verification_type":"generated","verification_ref":"check_affected_ases_matches_cycle","verification":"A grader can verify this by confirming affected_ases is a non-empty list of AS numbers that includes at least the ASNs reported in oscillation_cycle (65002 and 65003).","notes":"Not independently asserted by the verifier beyond key presence; this checks content correctness.","validation":{"item_id":"OSC-02","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"LEAK-01","requirement":"Correctly detect the BGP route leak that violates valley-free routing by setting route_leak_detected to true and populating route_leaks with at least one entry containing the fields leaker_as, source_as, destination_as, source_type, and destination_type.","source_quote":"Detect in the topology: oscillation and/or route leak event violating BGP valley-free routing","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestDetection::test_route_leak_detected","verification":"A grader can verify this by checking output_data['route_leak_detected'] is true, output_data['route_leaks'] is a non-empty list, and its first element contains all five required fields.","notes":"The verifier checks field presence on the first leak entry, not the specific AS numbers or relationship-type values.","validation":{"item_id":"LEAK-01","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"SOL-01","requirement":"For every solution listed in possible_solutions.json, add an entry to solution_results keyed by the exact solution text, with oscillation_resolved true only if the solution breaks the routing-preference cycle in the topology, and route_leak_resolved true only if the solution stops hub1/hub2 from advertising routes to hub2/hub1 via Virtual WAN.","source_quote":"For each solution, determine if it resolves oscillation and/or route leaks. To resolve oscillations, it must break the routing preference cycle in topology. To resolve route leaks, it must stop hub1/hub2 advertising routes to hub2/hub1 via Virtual Wan","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestSolutionEvaluation::test_solution_classification","verification":"A grader can verify this by iterating the 19 solutions in possible_solutions.json, confirming each exact solution string is a key in solution_results, and comparing its oscillation_resolved/route_leak_resolved booleans against the expected classification for that solution (10 solutions false/false, 3 true/false, 4 false/true, 2 true/true).","notes":"Includes the edge case 'disable hub peering between vhubvnet1 and vhubvnet2', which is expected false/false since severing peering does not break the preference cycle or stop leaked advertisements through Virtual WAN.","validation":{"item_id":"SOL-01","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}}],"runs":[{"id":"claude-code-no-skills__aws-bedrock-anthropic-claude-opus-4-7||azure-bgp-oscillation-route-leak","label":"claude-code-no-skills · aws-bedrock-anthropic-claude-opus-4-7","condition":"without skill","official":0.0,"raw":{"yes":5,"no":0,"abstain":0,"score":1.0,"coverage":1.0},"raw_answers":[{"item_id":"OUT-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"OSC-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"OSC-02","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"LEAK-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"SOL-01","answer":"YES"}],"anchored":{"yes":5,"no":1,"abstain":0,"score":0.8333333333333334,"coverage":1.0},"anchored_answers":[{"item_id":"OUT-01","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"OSC-01","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"OSC-02","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"LEAK-01","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"SOL-01","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"}],"raw_note":"","raw_source":null,"source":"main_table/leaderboard_all/results.jsonl:243","truncated":false},{"id":"claude-code-with-skills__aws-bedrock-anthropic-claude-opus-4-7||azure-bgp-oscillation-route-leak","label":"claude-code-with-skills · aws-bedrock-anthropic-claude-opus-4-7","condition":"with skill","official":0.0,"raw":{"yes":4,"no":1,"abstain":0,"score":0.8,"coverage":1.0},"raw_answers":[{"item_id":"OUT-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"OSC-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"OSC-02","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"LEAK-01","answer":"YES"},{"item_id":"SOL-01","answer":"NO"}],"anchored":{"yes":4,"no":2,"abstain":0,"score":0.6666666666666666,"coverage":1.0},"anchored_answers":[{"item_id":"OUT-01","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"OSC-01","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"OSC-02","answer":"YES","basis":"log-judgment"},{"item_id":"LEA